# Analyst Notes

Command Prompt remains one of the most frequently abused Windows utilities during post-exploitation. While many executions are legitimate, monitoring `cmd.exe` provides valuable visibility into attacker behavior, especially when correlated with other detections such as PowerShell execution, registry modifications, scheduled task creation, or network discovery.

This detection forms an important part of endpoint visibility and should be used alongside additional behavioral analytics to identify malicious command-line activity.
